//
// @IGNORE — DEFECT (both backends, 18594597b): a block whose tail is a slice is typed as the
//   iterator the slice lowers from.  `b = { src[1..3] }` is an internal compiler error, "index
//   out of bounds: the len is 0 but the index is 18446744073709551615 [src/scopes/scan.rs:272]"
//   (the slice's `break` reaches the scopes pass outside any loop), with and without an
//   annotation on `b`.  An `if` arm of the same slice is materialised (loft#1941).
//
// A SLICE AS A BLOCK TAIL IS A FRESH VECTOR (`@FR-Slice-Value` crossed with `@FR-H-Alloc`).
// "The value is owed at EVERY vector-typed position, not only a bind: … a block tail … take[s]
// the slice as the fresh vector a bind would make of it."  So the block answers a fresh
// vector (H-Alloc) of the slice's length, and a write into it does not reach the source.
//
// Values hand-computed from `src = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]`.
//
// @falsified-at: none — written against a live defect; it fails on 18594597b on both backends.
// CHANNEL: the compile (an internal compiler error), then the asserts.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: each message prints the values.
// HOLDS: `a-slice-is-a-fresh-value-at-every-vector-position` beside it.

fn main() {
  src = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50];
  b = {
    x = 1;
    src[x..x + 2]
  };
  b[1] = 55;
  assert(b.len() == 2 && b[0] == 20 && b[1] == 55 && src[2] == 30, "the block's slice: {b} {src}");
}
